To enhance user-friendliness, I will first modify error messages in errorHandler.js. Then, I'll implement a paraphrasing function in utils/paraphrase.js. Here's the updated code:

```javascript
// src/errorHandler.js
function handleError(error) {
    const userFriendlyMessage = paraphraseError(error.message);
    console.error(userFriendlyMessage);
    return userFriendlyMessage;
}

// src/utils/paraphrase.js
function paraphraseError(message) {
    const paraphrases = {
        'Unable to connect to database': 'We are having trouble reaching the database. Please check your connection.',
        'Permission denied': 'It seems you don’t have the required permissions to access this resource.',
    };
    return paraphrases[message] || message;
}
```
I also updated the README.md to reflect these changes and run tests to make sure everything works correctly.
